# Process Excellence Library — Quick Reference
# Full document: PROCESS_EXCELLENCE_LIBRARY.md (in project root or Chazwazza core)
# Version: 1.2.0 | Source: 55+ CEO influence patterns, 11 Universal Principles

## Universal Principles (Apply to ALL stages, ALL actions)

### UP-1: Investigation Before Action
Never modify anything until you fully understand the current state. Read before writing.
If uncertain, report findings and ask — don't assume and act.

### UP-2: Prevention Over Mitigation
When fixing a problem, eliminate the CLASS of problem, not just this instance.
Ask: "What systemic change prevents this entire class of issue?"

### UP-3: The Automation Principle
If you can run it, run it. Never provide CLI instructions for the user to copy-paste
when you have the capability to execute directly. Humans decide. Agents execute.

### UP-4: System-of-Record Discipline
Every piece of data has ONE canonical source. Write to and read from that source only.
Snapshots and caches are read-only. ACTION_ITEMS.yaml is a snapshot — use the API.

### UP-5: Quality Over Speed
Prioritize by architectural fit, risk, and adherence to enterprise best practice.
Never prioritize by effort or time. Detail now saves rework later.

### UP-6: Resource Consciousness
Token spend is a resource. Allocate toward highest-value work.
If blocked after reasonable effort, pivot — don't persist.

### UP-7: Test Before Production
No change reaches production without verification in a non-production environment.
Verify visually (Article 7 SEE) before declaring success.

### UP-8: Parallel Execution Awareness
When blocked (CI running, deployment in progress), switch to independent work.
Idle time is wasted time. But never start conflicting parallel work (Article 10 ONE).

### UP-9: Scope Hygiene
Know the current task boundary. Related work discovered during execution → log as separate task.
When the user pauses you, stop immediately and wait.

### UP-10: Product Boundary Awareness
Features belong in one product, not both. Data flows between products; screens don't duplicate.
When a feature could live in either product, escalate — don't assume.

### UP-11: Root Cause Convergence
Before asking "Why?", verify with the stakeholder that the behaviour IS wrong and agree on
which boundary is violated. 5 Whys drills depth; Convergence ensures correct direction.
A technically accurate observation is not a root cause unless the behaviour it describes is
actually incorrect. PNEUMA tells ("probably", "almost certainly") during diagnosis =
branch-selection errors. Verify before drilling.

