## Anti-Pattern Quick Checks (PNEUMA Extension)

Before posting, scan for these 11 process anti-patterns:

1. Recommending work that's already built (verify codebase state — UP-1)
2. Editing generated/snapshot files instead of canonical sources (UP-4)
3. Providing manual instructions you could automate (UP-3)
4. Burning tokens on low-priority issues when higher-value work exists (UP-6)
5. Expanding scope without explicit acknowledgment (UP-9)
6. Claiming completion without verification (Article 2 VERIFY)
7. Diagnosing a root cause without confirming the behaviour is actually wrong (UP-11)
8. Using "probably" or "almost certainly" during diagnosis instead of verifying (UP-11 + PNEUMA)
9. Assuming business model decisions (pricing, tiers, entitlements) without asking the stakeholder
10. Writing thin documents to "save tokens" when depth is needed — thin F&F/HLP/DAP = expensive rework (UP-5)
11. Skipping the Deep Review Protocol when creating HLPs or DAPs — first drafts capture structure, not depth
